2026-10-28T17:23:02.5712308Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H6WgmwUAdrNH2gnoTM9T8e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 13,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/13\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"[New Resource]: aws_datazone_project_profile resource\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### What new functionality are you requesting?\\n\\nA new resource, `aws_datazone_project_profile`, to manage Amazon DataZone / SageMaker Unified Studio project profiles.\\n\\n**This is not `aws_datazone_environment_profile`.** Environment profiles are a DataZone V1 concept and already exist in the provider. Project profiles are the V2 / SageMaker Unified Studio object, backed by a different API (`CreateProjectProfile`) and a different CloudFormation type (`AWS::DataZone::ProjectProfile`)\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nA project profile is the template every SageMaker Unified Studio project is created from. It declares which blueprints (capabilities) a project gets, **in which deployment mode**, with which parameter overrides, and which AWS account and region the resulting projects land in. It is the central object of a Unified Studio deployment \\u2014 the domain is the container, the blueprints are the inventory, and the project profile is the thing an end user actually consumes.\\n\\nThere is no equivalent in the `aws` provider. A complete Unified Studio deployment is currently impossible without `awscc`.\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n### Minimal usage\\n\\nBlueprint IDs resolve through the existing `aws_datazone_environment_blueprint` data source, so no new lookup mechanism is needed:\\n\\n```terraform\\ndata \\\"aws_caller_identity\\\" \\\"current\\\" {}\\ndata \\\"aws_region\\\" \\\"current\\\" {}\\n\\ndata \\\"aws_datazone_environment_blueprint\\\" \\\"tooling\\\" {\\n  domain_id = aws_datazone_domain.example.id\\n  name      = \\\"Tooling\\\"\\n  managed   = true\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_datazone_project_profile\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  domain_identifier      = aws_datazone_domain.example.id\\n  domain_unit_identifier = aws_datazone_domain.example.root_domain_unit_id\\n  name                   = \\\"research\\\"\\n  description            = \\\"Research project profile\\\"\\n  status                 = \\\"ENABLED\\\"\\n\\n  environment_configurations {\\n    name                     = \\\"Tooling\\\"\\n    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.tooling.id\\n    deployment_mode          = \\\"ON_CREATE\\\"\\n    deployment_order         = 0\\n\\n    aws_account {\\n      aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id\\n    }\\n\\n    aws_region {\\n      region_name = data.aws_region.current.name\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### The pattern this resource is needed for: on-demand capabilities with a pinned cost ceiling\\n\\n```terraform\\nlocals {\\n  blueprints = [\\\"Tooling\\\", \\\"RedshiftServerless\\\", \\\"MLExperiments\\\"]\\n}\\n\\ndata \\\"aws_datazone_environment_blueprint\\\" \\\"this\\\" {\\n  for_each  = toset(local.blueprints)\\n  domain_id = aws_datazone_domain.example.id\\n  name      = each.key\\n  managed   = true\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_datazone_project_profile\\\" \\\"research\\\" {\\n  domain_identifier      = aws_datazone_domain.example.id\\n  domain_unit_identifier = aws_datazone_domain_unit.research.id\\n  name                   = \\\"research\\\"\\n  status                 = \\\"ENABLED\\\"\\n\\n  # Mandatory floor: provisioned with every project\\n  environment_configurations {\\n    name                     = \\\"Tooling\\\"\\n    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.tooling.id\\n    deployment_mode          = \\\"ON_CREATE\\\"\\n    deployment_order         = 0\\n\\n    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }\\n    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }\\n  }\\n\\n  # Offered but not provisioned until a user asks, with the cost ceiling pinned\\n  environment_configurations {\\n    name                     = \\\"RedshiftServerless\\\"\\n    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.redshift.id\\n    deployment_mode          = \\\"ON_DEMAND\\\"\\n\\n    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }\\n    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }\\n\\n    configuration_parameters {\\n      parameter_overrides {\\n        name        = \\\"redshiftBaseCapacity\\\"\\n        value       = \\\"8\\\"\\n        is_editable = false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  environment_configurations {\\n    name                     = \\\"MLExperiments\\\"\\n    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.ml_experiments.id\\n    deployment_mode          = \\\"ON_DEMAND\\\"\\n\\n    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }\\n    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nNote that `deployment_order` is set only on `ON_CREATE` entries \\u2014 on-demand capabilities have no project creation to be ordered within.\\n\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- API: `CreateProjectProfile`, `GetProjectProfile`, `UpdateProjectProfile`, `DeleteProjectProfile`, `ListProjectProfiles`\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datazone/latest/APIReference/API_CreateProjectProfile.html\\n- CloudFormation: `AWS::DataZone::ProjectProfile`\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-resource-datazone-projectprofile.html\\n- Prior art: `awscc_datazone_project_profile`\\n  https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/awscc/latest/docs/resources/datazone_project_profile\\n- SageMaker Unified Studio project profiles and deployment modes\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker-unified-studio/latest/adminguide/project-profiles.html\\n- Related, already tracked:\\n  - `#50106` \\u2014 `aws_datazone_domain_unit` (a project profile's `domain_unit_identifier` needs it)\\n  - `#40891` \\u2014 `aws_datazone_group_profile` (groups must be registered before they can be granted use of a profile)\\n  - `#45198` \\u2014 `aws_datazone_project` missing V2 arguments (a project is created *from* a project profile)\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [],\n10\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:17Z\",\n11\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-22T09:16:25Z\"\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2de9b2b1-ee36-421e-a6cc-27fb255aa354","uuid":"a7c7467a-b90d-473c-aa79-d26938466315","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:23:02.564Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 13,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/13\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"[New Resource]: aws_datazone_project_profile resource\",\n  \"body\": \"### What new functionality are you requesting?\\n\\nA new resource, `aws_datazone_project_profile`, to manage Amazon DataZone / SageMaker Unified Studio project profiles.\\n\\n**This is not `aws_datazone_environment_profile`.** Environment profiles are a DataZone V1 concept and already exist in the provider. Project profiles are the V2 / SageMaker Unified Studio object, backed by a different API (`CreateProjectProfile`) and a different CloudFormation type (`AWS::DataZone::ProjectProfile`)\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nA project profile is the template every SageMaker Unified Studio project is created from. It declares which blueprints (capabilities) a project gets, **in which deployment mode**, with which parameter overrides, and which AWS account and region the resulting projects land in. It is the central object of a Unified Studio deployment \\u2014 the domain is the container, the blueprints are the inventory, and the project profile is the thing an end user actually consumes.\\n\\nThere is no equivalent in the `aws` provider. A complete Unified Studio deployment is currently impossible without `awscc`.\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n### Minimal usage\\n\\nBlueprint IDs resolve through the existing `aws_datazone_environment_blueprint` data source, so no new lookup mechanism is needed:\\n\\n```terraform\\ndata \\\"aws_caller_identity\\\" \\\"current\\\" {}\\ndata \\\"aws_region\\\" \\\"current\\\" {}\\n\\ndata \\\"aws_datazone_environment_blueprint\\\" \\\"tooling\\\" {\\n  domain_id = aws_datazone_domain.example.id\\n  name      = \\\"Tooling\\\"\\n  managed   = true\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_datazone_project_profile\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  domain_identifier      = aws_datazone_domain.example.id\\n  domain_unit_identifier = aws_datazone_domain.example.root_domain_unit_id\\n  name                   = \\\"research\\\"\\n  description            = \\\"Research project profile\\\"\\n  status                 = \\\"ENABLED\\\"\\n\\n  environment_configurations {\\n    name                     = \\\"Tooling\\\"\\n    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.tooling.id\\n    deployment_mode          = \\\"ON_CREATE\\\"\\n    deployment_order         = 0\\n\\n    aws_account {\\n      aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id\\n    }\\n\\n    aws_region {\\n      region_name = data.aws_region.current.name\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### The pattern this resource is needed for: on-demand capabilities with a pinned cost ceiling\\n\\n```terraform\\nlocals {\\n  blueprints = [\\\"Tooling\\\", \\\"RedshiftServerless\\\", \\\"MLExperiments\\\"]\\n}\\n\\ndata \\\"aws_datazone_environment_blueprint\\\" \\\"this\\\" {\\n  for_each  = toset(local.blueprints)\\n  domain_id = aws_datazone_domain.example.id\\n  name      = each.key\\n  managed   = true\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_datazone_project_profile\\\" \\\"research\\\" {\\n  domain_identifier      = aws_datazone_domain.example.id\\n  domain_unit_identifier = aws_datazone_domain_unit.research.id\\n  name                   = \\\"research\\\"\\n  status                 = \\\"ENABLED\\\"\\n\\n  # Mandatory floor: provisioned with every project\\n  environment_configurations {\\n    name                     = \\\"Tooling\\\"\\n    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.tooling.id\\n    deployment_mode          = \\\"ON_CREATE\\\"\\n    deployment_order         = 0\\n\\n    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }\\n    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }\\n  }\\n\\n  # Offered but not provisioned until a user asks, with the cost ceiling pinned\\n  environment_configurations {\\n    name                     = \\\"RedshiftServerless\\\"\\n    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.redshift.id\\n    deployment_mode          = \\\"ON_DEMAND\\\"\\n\\n    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }\\n    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }\\n\\n    configuration_parameters {\\n      parameter_overrides {\\n        name        = \\\"redshiftBaseCapacity\\\"\\n        value       = \\\"8\\\"\\n        is_editable = false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  environment_configurations {\\n    name                     = \\\"MLExperiments\\\"\\n    environment_blueprint_id = data.aws_datazone_environment_blueprint.ml_experiments.id\\n    deployment_mode          = \\\"ON_DEMAND\\\"\\n\\n    aws_account { aws_account_id = data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id }\\n    aws_region { region_name = data.aws_region.current.name }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nNote that `deployment_order` is set only on `ON_CREATE` entries \\u2014 on-demand capabilities have no project creation to be ordered within.\\n\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- API: `CreateProjectProfile`, `GetProjectProfile`, `UpdateProjectProfile`, `DeleteProjectProfile`, `ListProjectProfiles`\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datazone/latest/APIReference/API_CreateProjectProfile.html\\n- CloudFormation: `AWS::DataZone::ProjectProfile`\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-resource-datazone-projectprofile.html\\n- Prior art: `awscc_datazone_project_profile`\\n  https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/awscc/latest/docs/resources/datazone_project_profile\\n- SageMaker Unified Studio project profiles and deployment modes\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker-unified-studio/latest/adminguide/project-profiles.html\\n- Related, already tracked:\\n  - `#50106` \\u2014 `aws_datazone_domain_unit` (a project profile's `domain_unit_identifier` needs it)\\n  - `#40891` \\u2014 `aws_datazone_group_profile` (groups must be registered before they can be granted use of a profile)\\n  - `#45198` \\u2014 `aws_datazone_project` missing V2 arguments (a project is created *from* a project profile)\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:17Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-22T09:16:25Z\"\n}","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01H6WgmwUAdrNH2gnoTM9T8e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
